      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of successful non-operative treatment of coronary artery perforation that occurred during percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. The patient was receiving abciximab, aspirin and heparin. The perforation was recognized immediately and managed by partial reversal of heparin and inflation of a non-compliant balloon at the perforation site. The perforation sealed completely. The patient was discharged asymptomatic the following day."},
